{
  "id": "u03",
  "number": 3,
  "title": "Things and articles",
  "summary": "Name everyday things and say what they are. Learn every noun with its article: un, une, le, la, les and des.",
  "canDo": [
    "Name a thing with a or an: un livre, une table.",
    "Name a thing with the: le, la, l' or les.",
    "Talk about more than one thing, using des and plurals.",
    "Ask what something is, say what it is, and hand something over."
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u03-l1",
      "title": "A / an",
      "goal": "Name a thing with un or une, and learn each noun with its article.",
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": "u03-l1-n1",
          "title": "Every noun has a gender",
          "body": "In French, every noun is **masculine** or **feminine**, even things with no sex, like a table. You cannot work this out from the meaning, so learn each noun **with its article**: *un livre*, *une table*. The article is part of the word.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Un livre, s'il vous plaît.",
              "en": "A book, please."
            },
            {
              "fr": "Une table, madame ?",
              "en": "A table, madam?"
            },
            {
              "fr": "Un stylo, Paul ?",
              "en": "A pen, Paul?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u03-l1-n2",
          "title": "Un or une?",
          "body": "Both mean *a* (or *an*). Use **un** before a masculine noun and **une** before a feminine noun. Many feminine nouns end in **-e**, such as *une chaise*, but *un stylo* and *un sac* do not follow that pattern. Learn the article with the noun.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fr": "Une chaise, s'il te plaît.",
              "en": "A chair, please. (to a friend)"
            },
            {
              "fr": "Un sac, merci !",
              "en": "A bag, thanks!"
            },
            {
              "fr": "Une chaise, un sac.",
              "en": "A chair, a bag."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "words": [
